ercent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in 4.4.1.stable.official.49a5bc7b6\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.1.stable - Ubuntu 24.04.2 LTS 24.04 on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4060 (nvidia; 570.124.06) - 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i9-13900KS (32 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen using the compatibility renderer, a shader that reads the depth texture from inside a function called by fragment(), will not compile.\n\nError:\n```\nE 0:00:00:516   _display_error_with_code: SceneShaderGLES3: Fragment shader compilation failed:\n0(524) : error C1503: undefined variable \"depth_buffer\"\n\n  <C++ Source>  drivers/gles3/shader_gles3.cpp:265 @ _display_error_with_code()\n```\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCreate a compatibility renderer project, create a mesh with the shader\n```gdshader\nshader_type spatial;\nrender_mode unshaded, fog_disabled;\n\nuniform sampler2D depth_texture : hint_depth_texture, filter_nearest;\n\nfloat get_depth() {\n\treturn texture(depth_texture, vec2(0.0, 0.0)).r;\n}\n\nvoid vertex() {\n\tPOSITION = vec4(VERTEX.xy, 1.0, 1.0);\n}\n\nvoid fragment() {\n\tALBEDO = vec3(get_depth());\n}\n```\nRun the project\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[shader_error.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/21740875/shader_error.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/